From 0613e6b8f3e3b4a85ecbcf9b0bf41b098655d7d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:26:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Sign Cartouche's extensions with its own profile whenever
 SideStore signs it

The app SideStore is built into keeps its extensions, signed with its own
provisioning profile, when SideStore installs, updates or re-signs it, as
the Cartouche Installer signs it (isideload's ReuseMain): neither the
player's setting for app extensions nor the alert that asks applies.

An update passes the store's version of the app rather than its
InstalledApp, so it never read the choice that the InstalledApp keeps
(useMainProfile, which SideStore takes from the signature of the first
extension when it first meets the app it is built into), and registered
an App ID for each extension. LiveProcess, the extension Cartouche runs
its games and the built-in SideStore in, was then signed with an App ID
of its own, without the Increased Memory Limit that Cartouche's App ID
has: a game behind Cartouche's console had 3,376 MiB instead of 6,144 on
an iPhone with 12 GB, and 3,072 instead of 4,096 on one with 6 GB, from
the first update the built-in SideStore made until Cartouche was
installed again with the Installer. Renewals, which install profiles
without signing again, follow the InstalledApp, which the install
records, so that the next ones renew the main profile only, which
LiveProcess is then signed with.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MzPJotRoWqyfPs7d7YexEP
---
 .../RemoveAppExtensionsOperation.swift             | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/SideStore/Core/Operations/PipelineOperations/RemoveAppExtensionsOperation.swift b/SideStore/Core/Operations/PipelineOperations/RemoveAppExtensionsOperation.swift
index 22222a9..118c516 100644
--- a/SideStore/Core/Operations/PipelineOperations/RemoveAppExtensionsOperation.swift
+++ b/SideStore/Core/Operations/PipelineOperations/RemoveAppExtensionsOperation.swift
@@ -74,6 +74,20 @@ final class RemoveAppExtensionsOperation: BasePipelineOperation<InstallAppOperat
             return targetAppBundle
         }
         
+        // Cartouche: the app SideStore is built into keeps its extensions, signed with its
+        // own provisioning profile, as the Cartouche Installer signs them. LiveProcess, the
+        // extension Cartouche runs its games and this SideStore in, needs the Increased
+        // Memory Limit of Cartouche's App ID, which an App ID of its own never had: an
+        // update, which passes the store's version, never read the choice Cartouche's
+        // InstalledApp keeps, and registered an App ID for each extension. Needs proper
+        // testing on a phone.
+        if targetAppBundle.isAltStoreApp {
+            self.debugLog("[RemoveAppExtensionsOperation] Keeping the extensions of \(targetAppBundle.bundleIdentifier), signed with its own profile.")
+            self.context.useMainProfile = true
+            self.setProgress(100)
+            return targetAppBundle
+        }
+        
         self.setProgress(30)
         let excessExtensions = processExtensionsInfo(from: targetAppBundle, localAppExtensions: localAppExtensions)
         
